      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2015 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "Diabetics, particularly insulin treated, have increased risk of ischemic events and bleeding with percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI). The relative risk of atherothrombotic versus bleeding events is higher in diabetics than non-diabetics. Bivalirudin with provisional IIb/IIIa therapy has less bleeding and lower one-year mortality than routine IIb/IIIa therapy in diabetics undergoing PCI. IIb/IIIa agents should be reserved for provisional and niche applications during PCI."
      },
